PKGCHK(1)

# NAME

pkgchk - audit installed package objects

# SYNOPSIS

*pkgchk* [-Vh] [-r _root-dir_] {-l | -d | -a} [_package_ ...]

# DESCRIPTION

*pkgchk* is the reference frontend for *libpkgaudit*(3).  It reads one
immutable installed-state snapshot through libpkgstate, converts that
snapshot into the independent audit model, observes the selected root,
and presents the resulting facts.

If no package names are supplied, all installed packages are audited.
Exactly one audit mode is required.

# OPTIONS

*-l*, *--links*
	Check symlink resolution and ownership.

*-d*, *--disappeared*
	Check object presence and durable directory/non-directory class.

*-a*, *--audit*
	Run all checks.

*-r* _root-dir_, *--root*=_root-dir_
	Read _root-dir_/var/lib/pkg/db and inspect objects beneath
	_root-dir_.  The default is /.

*-v*
	Increase presentation detail.  Repeatable.

*-V*, *--version*
	Print version information and exit.

*-h*, *--help*
	Print usage and exit.

# EXIT STATUS

*0*
	The audit completed without integrity findings.

*1*
	The audit completed and reported integrity findings.

*2*
	Command usage, installed state, filesystem observation, or backend
	contract prevented a complete audit.

Ownership relations are advisory and do not by themselves change the
exit status.

# DESIGN

libpkgstate is linked by this executable, not by libpkgaudit.  Severity,
diagnostic text, verbosity, and exit status are frontend policy.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgaudit*(3), *pkginfo*(1)

